# Дано: 8 bots at 20-40 m from A, each walking; 8 x ~35 B x 30 Hz is far over 2048 B/s, so the budget defers.
# The budget is per connection and per second: no line for A over it; the nearest bot keeps its band's period; none of
# the eight starves (the longest wait of a relevant, changing pawn of A's connection stays within 60 steps).
Ждать server 60 6x \[Server\] net rates
Всегда server \[Server\] net rates.*player {a1}: (\d+) B/s <= {budget1}
Число server \[Server\] net rates.*player {a1}: [^;]*deferred (\d+) > 0
Всегда server \[Server\] net rates.*player {a1}: [^;]*longest wait (\d+) step <= 60
Число A \[Net\] pawn {bp1} \(player \d+\): (?:[1-4]?\d) m, period (\d+) == 2
Ждать A 30 fresh \[Net\] interpolation buffer: .*\(0 snap\(s\)\)
Тогда A verbs_budget all eight mannequins in A's view, each exactly one, feet on the ground, walking its circle; none frozen (_next shows each one step of walk further); the server's "net rates" line of the same second: "player <A>: <= 2048 B/s ... deferred > 0, longest wait <= 60 step(s)"
# Когда: B1 stops on its console, then walks on. Its pawn goes dormant (unchanged) on the server; its heading is
# kept (not turned to -Z); its interpolation delay in A's log is the same before the stop and after the walk.
Консоль B1 stop
Ждать B1 5 console: stopped at step
Ждать server 60 player \d+: pawn {bp1} dormant
Ждать A 10 fresh \[Net\] pawn {bp1} \(player \d+\): .*delay \d+\.\d+ s
Запомнить r0 A \[Net\] pawn {bp1} \(player \d+\): .*delay (\d+\.\d+) s
Тогда A verbs_stop B1 stands where it stopped, one mannequin on the ground, facing the way it walked (B1's log "console: stopped ... facing N deg"; its shoulders not turned to -Z against verbs_budget, the frame before the stop); _next identical; the other seven walk on; server log "pawn <B1> dormant"
Консоль B1 walk
Ждать B1 5 console: walk resumed at step
Ждать server 30 pawn {bp1} awake
Ждать A 10 fresh \[Net\] pawn {bp1} \(player \d+\): .*delay \d+\.\d+ s
Запомнить r1 A \[Net\] pawn {bp1} \(player \d+\): .*delay (\d+\.\d+) s
Сверить r0 r1 0.03
Тогда A verbs_resume B1 walks on along its circle from where it stopped: one mannequin, no jump back, no second mannequin left at the stop, feet on the ground; _next shows it one frame of walk further; A's log: B1's delay before the stop and after the walk equal within 30 ms (r0/r1)
# Когда: B2's next three Input messages are cut to two bytes (the server drops each as malformed and the input is
# sent again), then its next thirty Snapshot messages are dropped on receipt (the acks stop, the unacked inputs grow,
# and drain once snapshots arrive again). The session survives both.
# None before the fault: every "malformed Input dropped" after it is one of B2's three.
Нет server connection \d+: malformed Input dropped
Консоль B2 corrupt Input 3
Ждать server 10 3x connection \d+: malformed Input dropped
Ждать B2 5 fault done: corrupt Input x3
Ждать B2 5 fresh unacked inputs [0-9], ack step
Нет B2 session closed
Консоль B2 drop Snapshot 30
Ждать B2 5 unacked inputs (?:1[5-9]|[2-9]\d),
Ждать B2 10 fault done: drop Snapshot x30
Ждать B2 5 fresh unacked inputs [0-9],
Нет B2 session closed
Нет server connection \d+: malformed Snapshot
Ждать A 30 fresh \[Net\] interpolation buffer: .*\(0 snap\(s\)\)
Тогда A verbs_fault B2 walks its circle, one mannequin, feet on the ground (no jump, no ghost after the dropped snapshots); the server logged exactly three "malformed Input dropped" and no "malformed Snapshot"; B2's log "unacked inputs 0-9" again and no "session closed"
Нет A \(([1-9]\d*) snap\(s\)\)
Нет server malformed ViewReport
